        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "LOCATION\n\nConveniently positioned just 6.5kms south of Westport in beautiful west Mayo along the Wild Atlantic Way. Located with good road access to the N59 providing easy access to Westport town centre or southwards onto Leenane and Connemara. This property sits along a quiet country lane shared by only 5 homes and surrounded by farmland. This is a quiet and idyllic country setting close to a host of amenities including forest walks, local shop with filling station, garage and café.\n\nWestport is a charming coastal town on the inner shores of Clew Bay. Long renowned as a centre of tourism, it attracts thousands of visitors annually who are attracted to its warm people, lively ambiances, local artisan food producers, excellent bars, restaurants and cafés. Westport is also home to several key international employers including Allergan/ AbbVie, Portwest and Carraig Donn. The town and indeed the region is blessed with its stunning scenery with Clew Bay, Croagh Patrick and the Nephin Mountains.\n\nLocal attractions include Westport House Estate, The Greenway, championship golf, excellent freshwater fishing and sea angling, numerous Blue Flag beaches and its lively nightlife. Westport is well connected with road and rail being on the N5, N59 and main Westport to Dublin rail with several services daily.\n\nWestport 6.5kms, Galway 83kms, Dublin 258km, Ireland West Airport 61kms\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\nA one-off truly unique home which was built in 2003. Designed by award winning London-based Architects, this home has been crafted and beautifully built to provide bright spacious accommodation mainly over ground floor but with a first floor master bedroom.\n\nExtending to 220 sq.m. (2,368 sq.ft), the property is built on the site of a former period cottage and constructed of traditional concrete block walls finished with a mix of painted render and cedar cladding, all under a slate pitched roof. Windows are double glazed painted artic pine. Indeed extensive use of glazing including a wonderful corridor to the front of the home floods the property with light.\n\nFinishes throughout are excellent and include extensive use of tile, large open plan kitchen and dining room, open plan living room with wood burning stove, glazed corridor leading to external patio, three downstairs bedrooms, one ensuite and large family bathroom. At first floor there is the master ensuite bedroom.\n\nFEATURES:\n\n•Located just 6.5kms south of Westport close to N59 (Leenane Road) \n•Totally unique Architect designed 4 bed home extending to 220sq.m (2,368 sq.ft)\n•Site area of 0.26 Hectares (0.64 Acres) which is landscaped\n•Beautifully appointed light filled accommodation throughout\n•Walk in condition with double glazing and OFCH\n•Ample on site car parking\n\nSITE\n\nThe property sits on a land holding of 0.26 Hectares (0.65 Acres). Lovely garden to front with sheltered patio, gravel drive to rear leading to large open plan main garden which is bordered to the west by a small stream. All boundaries are in dry stone walls.\n\n \nSERVICES\n\nThe property has the following services:-\n\nWater- Group water scheme\nSewerage- On-site treatment plant\nElectricity- Mains provider\nTelecoms- Broadband/WI-FI\n\nTITLE\n\nFreehold title held within Folio MY18645F.\n\n\nACCOMMODATION COMPRISES: \n \nGROUND FLOOR\n\nENTRANCE HALL:20.73m x 1.89m\nTiled floor, extensive ceiling mounted light well, number of doors onto front garden\n\nLIVING ROOM:5.6m x 4.51m\nTile floor, large wood burning stove, built-in shelves\n\nKITCHEN/DINER11.18m x 4.58m\nOpen plan, tiled floor, double doors to rear garden, extensive high polished white kitchen with Corian work surfaces, integrated 5 ring Siemens electric hob and Zanussi oven, built-in pantry, extensive light well to ceiling\n\nUTILITY ROOM:3.27m x 2.98m\nCounter with integrated sink, shelving units\n\nHALLWAY:1.83m x 4.72m\n\n\nBATHROOM:4.0m x 2.23m\nFully tiled walls and floor, sunken bath, whb, wc, large double power shower, integrated Velux to ceiling\n\nBEDROOM (1):4.84m x 3.76m\nSolid oak floors\n\nBEDROOM (2):3.43m x 4.51m\nSolid oak floors. Includes EN SUITE SHOWER ROOM with tiled walls and floor, whb, wc, double shower, heated towel rail\n\n \nBEDROOM (3):3.26m x 4.51m\nSolid oak floors. Includes EN SUITE SHOWER ROOM with tiled walls and floor, wc, whb, double shower and heated towel rail\n\nFIRST FLOOR\nAccessed via carpeted timber staircase\n\nBEDROOM (4):6.16m x 4.65m\nRecessed spotlights to ceiling, built-in wardrobe space, vanity area. Includes EN SUITE SHOWER ROOM with wc\n\nASKING PRICE 650,000\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\nThis property sits along a quiet country lane off the N59 just 6.5kms south of Westport . Follow google map directions for Eircode F28 XN28.\n"
